      <article class="legal-card">
        <section class="legal-section">
          <span class="legal-kicker">What We Collect</span>
          <h2>Contact details tied to your booking.</h2>
          <p>Seascape Vacations currently collects the information needed to handle bookings and guest communication. The live site policy covers three core fields:</p>
          <ul class="legal-list">
            <li>your name</li>
            <li>your email address</li>
            <li>your phone number</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <span class="legal-kicker">How We Use It</span>
          <h3>Booking support and a better site experience.</h3>
          <p>We use that information to process bookings and improve your experience with Seascape Vacations.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <span class="legal-kicker">Site Analytics</span>
          <h3>GA4 and Seascape conversion events stay on.</h3>
          <p>The site uses Google Analytics 4 and Seascape's own conversion tracking to understand page visits, direct-booking clicks, email signups, and owner inquiry actions. Meta Pixel has been removed, and the site does not use PostHog.</p>
          <p>Analytics events are scrubbed so names, email addresses, phone numbers, message notes, and property addresses are not sent in GA4 or dataLayer event payloads.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <span class="legal-kicker">Third-Party Sale</span>
          <h3>We do not sell your data.</h3>
          <p>The current Seascape policy is simple: we do not sell your information to third parties.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <span class="legal-kicker">Security</span>
          <h3>Your information is stored securely.</h3>
          <p>Seascape Vacations states that your data is encrypted and stored securely.</p>
        </section>
      </article>

